## 11. Technical Architecture 🔧

### Core Data Structures
```typescript
interface PlayerCard {
  // Identity
  characterName: string
  level: number
  experience: number
  theme: ThemeDefinition
  
  // Performance Metrics
  totalKeystrokes: number
  currentStreak: number
  averageKMP: number
  qualityScore: number
  
  // Collection Data
  cards: CardInstance[]
  unlockedPacks: PackType[]
  activeDeck: CardInstance[]
  
  // Progression
  customFormulas: FormulaSet
  achievementHistory: Achievement[]
  milestoneProgress: MilestoneTracker
}

interface CardInstance {
  id: string
  noteReference: string
  rarity: RarityTier
  isShiny: boolean
  powerLevel: number
  acquisitionDate: Date
  timesUsed: number
  enhancementLevel: number
}

interface PackOpening {
  packType: string
  openedAt: Date
  performanceContext: PerformanceSnapshot
  cardsReceived: CardInstance[]
  rarityBonuses: BonusModifier[]
}
```

### Performance Optimizations
**Real-Time Calculations:**
- Keystroke events throttled to prevent lag
- EXP calculations cached and batch-updated
- Card generation performed in background workers
- UI updates use requestAnimationFrame for smooth animations

**Memory Management:**
- Card collection stored efficiently with lazy loading
- Large pack opening animations use object pooling
- Performance history maintains rolling windows
- Automatic cleanup of old session data

**Vault Integration:**
- Note analysis performed incrementally during idle time
- Card mapping cache updated only when files change
- Relationship calculations use efficient graph algorithms
- Large vault support with pagination and filtering

